        "text": "The latest observed value is April at 544.44 thousand, which is below June 2025 at 547.70 thousand; the forecast point, not the latest observation, is above June 2025. A June seasonal normalization toward the historical June-November path offsets part of the recent decline, while the 6.6% May unemployment rate applies modest downside pressure."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: the model prior center is 554.44 thousand, using April persistence and the fetched local-level reference class. The explicit adjustments are +4.20 thousand for June seasonal normalization, -1.31 thousand for the lower May unemployment rate and recent April momentum, yielding 554.44 + 4.20 - 1.31 = 557.33 thousand. Successive changes across the fetched level history give sigma = 7.84 thousand, so the nominal 80% half-width is roughly 1.28*sigma = 10.04 thousand. The ladder-implied half-width is 16.31 thousand, or 1.63 times the volatility width; this widening reflects the missing May observation, unreleased June labour-market information, and the observed reversals in the level series."
